  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Independent Monitoring and Evaluation, Learning and Research (TPVM&amp;R)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MERL to provide services for two complementary programmes. First, the FCDO bilateral development programme Evidence for Health Programme (E4H) in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP), Punjab and at the Federal level (PART ONE of ToRs); and second the World Bank-funded the National Health Support Programme (NHSP) (PART TWO of ToRs). As major World Bank shareholder and contributor to the Global Funds the UK has an active interest in National Health Support Programme (NHSP), in line with the overall approach to development outlined in the UK Strategy for International Development and in the UK-Pakistan Development Partnership Summary</narrative>
  </description>
